% The OTHER width cost, kept separate on purpose (M1-T30; D-0028's "a neighbouring
% cost, measured in passing and explicitly NOT covered here").
%
% A satisfiable model over wide domains: a + b = 99 and b - a = 1, with both
% variables declared 0..99. `indomain_min` descends one value at a time, so the
% search depth is Theta(w) and the proof is 545 lines of `rup` with nogoods that
% carry one decision literal per level, plus a `sol` line naming every order literal
% of the solution.
%
% Measured here, with veripb 3.0.2:
%
%                     .opb     .pbp    lines   `pol`   `rup`   max level
%   width_root_unsat  126 kB  23.9 kB      6       1       0       none
%   this model       16.1 kB  29.9 kB    545       0     293         49
%
% The two are the same size and share no mechanism whatever. width_root_unsat's
% proof is one enormous justification line for a derivation that never branched;
% this one's is a long thin tree of small lines with no justification arithmetic in
% it at all. D-0028 asks in as many words that a future measurement of "proof size
% versus domain width" not attribute this cost to its own -- so the suite now
% carries both, and they are labelled.
%
% Kept at w = 99, not 999. At 999 this shape is a 1.7 MB proof (D-0028) and would
% cost the gate more than the effect is worth; at 99 it is ~160 ms end to end and the
% Theta(w) depth is already plain (49 decision levels for a two-variable model).
%
% That figure was 43 ms when this header was written and is 150-170 ms now (five runs,
% 2026-09-21, M4-T3; peak RSS 8.8 MB). D-0062 bisected the change to one commit and
% ACCEPTED it, so this is the recorded new cost and not a regression to chase. The figure
% is corrected rather than deleted because a number with a date on it is the only reason
% the change was noticed at all.
array [1..2] of int: sum_c = [1, 1];
array [1..2] of int: diff_c = [-1, 1];
var 0..99: a :: output_var;
var 0..99: b :: output_var;
constraint int_lin_eq(sum_c, [a, b], 99);
constraint int_lin_eq(diff_c, [a, b], 1);
solve satisfy;
